  "meta": { "confirm": "dualshock2.cross", "cancel": "dualshock2.circle", "primary": "dualshock2.cross", "secondary": "dualshock2.square" },
  "_notes": "DualShock 2 face, d-pad and shoulder buttons are pressure-sensitive. PCSX2 reads that from the source's analog value, so they stay in 'buttons' (as on real hardware they act as digital in most games); a trigger source gives real pressure on l2/r2. Pressure on face buttons only works with an analog-face source, which no common pad has. The 'analog' button is unbound (PCSX2 handles analog mode). Guitar, Buzz and EyeToy devices are not modelled."
